-- A member has a late loan when a Loan naming it is due before today. This file spells the
-- member's loans as `Loan where member == this`.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", this line among others:
--
--   ### Member
--   - Time passing can now make a Member stop being a MemberWithLateLoan.
--
-- That cannot happen. A loan due before today stays due before today on every later day, and
-- time passing removes no loan. The same condition spelled `exists (loans where dueOn < today)`
-- does not draw the line.
act Member { name: text }

act Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

shape MemberWithLateLoan = Member where exists (Loan where member == this and dueOn < today)
